@startuml
title Topology — one engine, many subjects

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #666666
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #666666
}

actor "Document manager" as Operator

component "CMTAT token A" as TokenA
component "CMTAT token B" as TokenB
component "**DocumentEngine**" as Engine
database "documents,\nkeyed by subject" as Store

TokenA --> Engine : setDocument(name, ...)
TokenB --> Engine : setDocument(name, ...)
Operator --> Engine : setDocument(**subject**, name, ...)\nbindToken(token)
Engine --> Store

note right of TokenA
  **Bound-token path.** The token calls the
  single-argument ERC-1643 functions; the
  engine uses msg.sender as the subject, so
  a token can only touch its own documents.
end note

note right of Operator
  **Admin path.** Names the subject
  explicitly, so one manager can write
  for any contract in the fleet.
end note

@enduml
